This was the one I expected to find self-serving, because rewriting a test that
"pinned the defect" is where a convenient rewrite hides. It isn't.

The settle at `:12717` has no enclosing `if` and no upstream gate; the halt path
sets `converged = False` and `break`s, so control reaches it. And the central
claim is tool-confirmed rather than asserted: running the **pre-commit** test
file against the current runner **fails**, so the shipped test really did pin the
