The pattern is not carelessness. It is that **the claim and the fix are made in
one motion**, so the evidence gathered is the evidence that the mechanism *can*
fire — an instance — and the claim asserted is that it *does* fire — a
population. Instance and population are one keystroke apart in prose and a
denominator apart in fact.

**The single change: no claim without a denominator, and the denominator must be
produced by committed code.**

Concretely: any commit message asserting *"X now happens"* must carry the
command that enumerates the population and prints `k / n`, and that command must
be in the repo. Not "I checked and it works" — `python3 scripts/foo.py --check`
printing `711 pairs, 282 above threshold`. You already do this sometimes, and the
